{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded","id":465109,"title":"There's no \"I\" in Dragonblooded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-01T13:43:25-07:00","id":465109,"title":"There's no \"I\" in Dragonblooded","content":"So JayTee sparked off this idea. Since Solar charms are hopefully in their final form (until the charmset busts out and says &quot;Fools! This isn't even my final form!&quot;) what do you want from Derpinblooded and their teamwork effects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T13:47:55-07:00","id":465133,"title":"","content":"On the one hand, I really <i>really</i> love the image of the Dragon-Blooded as elemental power rangers who sally forth and fight the monster of the week while scheming, plotting and engaging in epic dramas in between battles. Teamwork effects really work with my mental image of them as the aristocratic legion Exalted.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if their powerset is too heavily entrenched in teamwork effects, it really cripples them in mixed games, which I believe are just as popular as all solar and all dragon blooded games. Balance between the two is the key, but how heavily one side should be weighted in favor of the other is currently up in the air in my mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T13:47:56-07:00","id":465134,"title":"","content":"I'd like some Lore/Occult charms that allow you to make good use of infrastructure. The Realm has <i>libraries</i>, you're not relegated to picking up scraps from old musty tomes found in ruins, there should be effects that tie in to having access to that sort of institutional support for your research.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T13:53:45-07:00","id":465144,"title":"","content":"Seduction/Wingman Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T14:04:44-07:00","id":465149,"title":"","content":"I'd like Dragonblooded team effects to take into account the individuality and personality of the Dragonblooded in the group. So it's like specific people with their own strengths coming together, rather than &quot;Insert Red DB here! Line up all the colours.&quot;. It's really important to me that individual Dragonblooded do not feel interchangeable with others.<br /> <br /> At the same time, I think the Dragonblooded should get something from being in groups, but they should be quite flexible to changes in group dynamics and to operating solo.<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded society has Sworn Brotherhoods, which are quite important, and of course they're like &quot;By Our Powers Combined!&quot; however they're also quite free agents and I see Dynastic society as quite fluid, in a (gulp) Game of Thrones-y way, in that alliances can change overnight, people can die, and all can be change. <br /> <br /> Obviously, this is not going to happen to PC groups as hard, still it's an important principle.<br /> <br /> Maybe some of this emerges naturally from an idea DBs tend more towards specialisation and specialists tending to get advantages from coordination, rather than specific Charm effects of an &quot;I am here to make you work together&quot; sort.<br /> <br /> I think to some degree you play off power from cooperation against difficulty of coordination.<br /> <br /> Re: specific Charm effects, Jutlander's post makes me think of coordinated social pressures / bureaucratic moves...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T15:10:03-07:00","id":465213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aretii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=465134#post465134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like some Lore/Occult charms that allow you to make good use of infrastructure. The Realm has <i>libraries</i>, you're not relegated to picking up scraps from old musty tomes found in ruins, there should be effects that tie in to having access to that sort of institutional support for your research.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to see more of this in general; Dragonblooded work together, but that shouldn't just mean they're good at teamwork in small groups. Institutions like libraries or schools or bureaucracies are how a whole society works together, and I'd like to see that reflected in their Charms. Not in the Solar &quot;create an institution ex nihilo&quot; sense, but in a more &quot;better/more efficient when contributing to or benefiting from an institution&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T15:28:33-07:00","id":465229,"title":"","content":"There is an I in Terrestrial, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T15:30:19-07:00","id":465231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=465229#post465229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is an I in Terrestrial, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there is an I in pie. There is also an I in meat pie, meat is an anagram of team so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T15:35:36-07:00","id":465250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=465213#post465213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see more of this in general; Dragonblooded work together, but that shouldn't just mean they're good at teamwork in small groups. Institutions like libraries or schools or bureaucracies are how a whole society works together, and I'd like to see that reflected in their Charms. Not in the Solar &amp;quot;create an institution ex nihilo&amp;quot; sense, but in a more &amp;quot;better/more efficient when contributing to or benefiting from an institution&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought of this a few weeks ago when I wanted to make a Solar who leverages the massive power of the bureaucracy that he works for, but then looking though their themes and charms I realized that Solar bureaucrats don't work for anybody, and their role in an organization is to take it over wholesale. <br /> <br /> I wanted to be a thinly bearded douchbag who taps his clipboard and referenced the giant book that his scribes carry around for him, but solars are just too...in charge at the top to really do that sadly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T16:25:06-07:00","id":465312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kongurous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=465229#post465229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is an I in Terrestrial, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also an l in Dragonblooded. Perhaps that's close enough to an I.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1551-barefoot-monkey","name":"Barefoot Monkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1551_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T16:52:22-07:00","id":465343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded#post465109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So JayTee sparked off this idea. Since Solar charms are hopefully in their final form (until the charmset busts out and says &quot;Fools! This isn't even my final form!&quot;) what do you want from Derpinblooded and their teamwork effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... Just to brainstorm a few<ul><li>Team combos</li> <li>Charms that change in effect if they are used on the same round as another charm</li> <li>More team defenses</li> <li>Group casting sorcery</li> <li>Charms which passively get better with more dragonblooded around</li> <li>Team attacks which provide bonuses besides simply numeric ones</li> </ul>I'm not really sure how any of those would work, but hey, just throwing those out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T17:06:57-07:00","id":465349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=465133#post465133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, if their powerset is too heavily entrenched in teamwork effects, it really cripples them in mixed games, which I believe are just as popular as all solar and all dragon blooded games. Balance between the two is the key, but how heavily one side should be weighted in favor of the other is currently up in the air in my mind</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this was the problem with pre-errata Sidereal Lore: presuming a single splat game, and thereby being worthless without having other Sids around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T17:22:21-07:00","id":465384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=465349#post465349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, this was the problem with pre-errata Sidereal Lore: presuming a single splat game, and thereby being worthless without having other Sids around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... Maybe it would be best if the Dragonblooded got generic teamwork charms. At the same time, Dragonblooded working better with each other than with others does fit the fluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T18:16:03-07:00","id":465428,"title":"","content":"Can always potentially combine the two. Teamwork charms that only partly count as charm-dice when working with DBs or something. That sort of thing; &quot;This works very well when you're working with others. It works even better when working with other Dragonblooded.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T18:30:41-07:00","id":465438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=465384#post465384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... Maybe it would be best if the Dragonblooded got generic teamwork charms. At the same time, Dragonblooded working better with each other than with others does fit the fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree. Dragonbloods work best in groups, but that ought not preclude them from being able to act without their brethren. The Terrestrial Host is empowered by the same energies that propel the world, why shouldn't they be able to bolster and invigorate those born within it?<br /> <br /> Besides, it would be a pretty poor conspiracy if the Bronze Faction decided that their linchpin catspaw could only play their A game with one another, and no one else, while all their opponents have no such restriction to their abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T18:56:04-07:00","id":465456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=465428#post465428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can always potentially combine the two. Teamwork charms that only partly count as charm-dice when working with DBs or something. That sort of thing; &quot;This works very well when you're working with others. It works even better when working with other Dragonblooded.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got the right idea! This exactly.<br /> <br /> A Terrestrial might can use a Charm to bolster one or more allies traits equal to his own. However, if it is used on another Dragon-Blooded, he may be able to reflexively activate the Charm as well (whether or not he has it) for a different trait. It gives a sense of...their powers don't just add together, they multiply!<br /> <br /> And of course, during active attacks as well. Perhaps a Charm that as long as the Dragon-Blooded has an ally fighting beside him, he gains a boost to his Accuracy and Defense per ally, up to his Essence. If its a Dragon-Blooded ally, he also gains that Terrestrial's Anima surrounding his weapon, as per Dragon-Graced Weapon.<br /> <br /> And another thing that might be cool is that it doesn't <i>have</i> to be an ally. By that I mean, as long as another Dragon-Blooded is nearby, you gain the effect, as the blood reacts to blood. Perhaps.<br /> <br /> Not entirely certain, but Im certainly excited to find out!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T19:06:58-07:00","id":465468,"title":"","content":"While it would be cool for Dragon-Blooded Occult to include a charm or two that makes group-working sorcery easier or more powerful, I really want to see group-casting and group-working as something any sorcerer can do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=465384#post465384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... Maybe it would be best if the Dragonblooded got generic teamwork charms. At the same time, Dragonblooded working better with each other than with others does fit the fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't there a Dragon-Blooded charm that gets more powerful when in the vicinity of the Anathema, so Wyld Hunts can use it as an especially &quot;holy&quot; weapon? Except it's actually a teamwork charm from the First Age to help Terrestrials work better in the proximity of their Celestial commanders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T19:10:14-07:00","id":465470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=465468#post465468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't there a Dragon-Blooded charm that gets more powerful when in the vicinity of the Anathema, so Wyld Hunts can use it as an especially &quot;holy&quot; weapon? Except it's actually a teamwork charm from the First Age to help Terrestrials work better in the proximity of their Celestial commanders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Defense from Anathema Method, otherwise known as Dragon's Parable Defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T19:39:51-07:00","id":465506,"title":"","content":"Given the fact that Charm trees are apparently immense now, there's no reason that all comers can't be satisfied here.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm clearly not an expert in Charm design, but if I were gonna build Dragon-Blooded trees the way I'd do it in one of two ways: I'd either make the usual logical Charm trees that proceed from root to branch in an understandable fashion, with logical branches, and bolt the synergy Charms on in ways that make them entirely skippable if you want to do so, but easily takeable without many speedbumps if you didn't. This would provide flexibility for people who wanted to be all &quot;I'm a Prince of the Earth, motherfuckers, not some <i>soldier</i>&quot; and also people who wanted to be all &quot;I am totally a soldier, all Princes of the Earth are soldiers, <i>that's why we exist</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> The other way you could do it is have Charms pull double-duty, which might be a whole lot more interesting. &quot;This Charm has Effect X if you use it when flying solo, but it also has the Synergy Keyword, when you use it in that way it has Effect Y, which is similar both mechanically and thematically to Effect X but is instead designed for teamwork purposes.&quot; Or something like that, anyway. Kind of like how they're projecting Getimian design, where Charms do different weird shit depending on what sort of Essence you dump in them.<br /> <br /> And of course there is always room for weird one-offs and suchly. The occasional Charm that's something like &quot;this Charm is actually really bland, not bad per se but doesn't do anything special, but if you hook up with people who have the explicit complementary Charms to it (which are also actually kind of bland) you plug together like Voltron and are suddenly really fucking powerful.&quot; You wouldn't want to do that too often, because that specific example is very &quot;you'd better be in an all-DB game with people who want to take the complementary Charms with you&quot; but it would be a way to mix it up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T20:07:01-07:00","id":465539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=465384#post465384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... Maybe it would be best if the Dragonblooded got generic teamwork charms. At the same time, Dragonblooded working better with each other than with others does fit the fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Generic teamwork Charms with stackable effects. Useful in mixed-Splat games but even more useful with other DB's.<br /> <br /> Apparently someone beat me to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T21:04:04-07:00","id":465600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded#post465109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So JayTee sparked off this idea. Since Solar charms are hopefully in their final form (until the charmset busts out and says &quot;Fools! This isn't even my final form!&quot;) what do you want from Derpinblooded and their teamwork effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>Voltron.<br /> <br /> I want to join with my circlemates into a giant elemental form I can use to wrestle/stab godzilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T02:41:09-07:00","id":465831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=465600#post465600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Voltron.<br /> <br /> I want to join with my circlemates into a giant elemental form I can use to wrestle/stab godzilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you imagining 1 of each aspect being required for this, or could we do Magicka-like combinations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1551-barefoot-monkey","name":"Barefoot Monkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1551_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T04:20:51-07:00","id":465913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=465144#post465144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seduction/Wingman Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is great, absolutely, but it also shows how I'd like DB charms to work when it comes to teamwork. A DB can be a great wingman, a DB can be very seductive, when they come together they just naturally work off each other.<br /> <br /> DB charms should have this &quot;you set them up, I'll knock them down&quot; feel, I think. And they don't even need to work off other DB charms, they could work off Solar charms, or imposed conditions caused by anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T06:40:02-07:00","id":466014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=465600#post465600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Voltron.<br /> <br /> I want to join with my circlemates into a giant elemental form I can use to wrestle/stab godzilla.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NiokMc7g0bk\" target=\"_blank\">I want to make a Big Emperor Form.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T10:26:17-07:00","id":466260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=465468#post465468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there a Dragon-Blooded charm that gets more powerful when in the vicinity of the Anathema, so Wyld Hunts can use it as an especially &quot;holy&quot; weapon? Except it's actually a teamwork charm from the First Age to help Terrestrials work better in the proximity of their Celestial commanders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Defense-From-Anathema Method/Dragon's Parable Defense has a bit of a strange history to it. The original wording in 1e and 2e Dragon-Blooded simply stated that it worked against &quot;Anathema,&quot; and didn't really go into any detail on what counted for that. When the Dragon-Blooded got the large errata overhaul that came with Thousand Correct Actions of the Upright Soldier, it got a clarification that explains that it worked against all creatures of darkness, plus Celestial Exalted, to cover Solar and Lunar Anathema. That was probably how most groups would run it, so it made sense, but it then had to explain <i>why</i> the holy protection charm would work against them. It attributed this to the Dragon-Blood tapping Gaia's primordial power and love as a shield. That introduces a lot of weird setting stuff (can I shut down Defense-From-Anathema by killing Gaia?) and also is pretty far away from the paradigm of how Terrestrial Charms work. So, when the Dreams of the First Age errata came around, it talked about how Defense-From-Anathema Method was known as Dragon's Parable Defense, like you described.<br /> <br /> That's sort of a twisted and tangled history, and I wouldn't want to use that kind of stopgap retcon as a foundation moving forward (even though I personally thought it was very clever).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T10:35:24-07:00","id":466262,"title":"","content":"I want Charms that interact with the physicality of a Dragon-Blooded's Anima. Animas have been so mechanically passive in the past, only integrated in stunts or passive bonuses. I'm thinking instead of Elemental repurchases having the same Charm no repurchase for everybody, but if you've got a swirly bunch of Elemental Fury about you, it does something specifically cooler or better actively, hopefully even out-of-Apsect.<br /> <br /> I want an Athletics Charm that benefits from being Earth-Aspected where the Earth Aspect literally walks up a stone staircase whose steps emerge from his Anima (increasing range or duration of an Athletics movement effect).<br /> <br /> I want a Melee Charm that benefits from being Water-Aspected where when an opponent parries the Water Aspect the Anima floods the opponent for knockdown.<br /> <br /> I want an Occult Charm that interacts with Spirits of living concepts (such as a social bonus) for being Wood-Aspected like a rabbit-spirit eating the Anima of a Wood Aspect as they converse.<br /> <br /> I want a War Charm that interacts with being Fire-Aspected such that I can light the arrows of my archers mid-flight through the force of my Anima, or perhaps extinguish incoming flaming arrows so long as my Anima is active.<br /> <br /> I want a Martial Arts Charm that interacts with being Air-Aspected where the Air Aspect can weaponize gusts of wind to alter his opponent's stance to be more open to her enhanced attack (some sort of DV penalty on top of the Charm bonus).<br /> <br /> I know those don't fit the Ability-Aspect matrix, but that's kind of my point, having neat reasons to go out of your Aspect Charmset, so that its worth the mote penalty, tied to the Anima getting involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T11:31:27-07:00","id":466314,"title":"","content":"In one of my very very few attempts to write charms, I made an idea for I dunno what ability that let a Terrestrial extend their anima powers to all their brotherhood. So for example a Water Aspect could use it to take their whole team under the sea and they could all breathe just fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T12:15:21-07:00","id":466355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=466260#post466260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Defense-From-Anathema Method/Dragon's Parable Defense has a bit of a strange history to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would just like to chime in here and say that Defense-From-Anathema Method is one of my favorite Charms, and its history of one of the few genuinely good and delightful things to come out of DotFA.<br /> <br /> It just works on a lot of levels. On the surface, it is an interesting and effective Charm that meshes well with the official ideology of the Realm and also stands to reason. Of course the Dragon-Blooded would have a widely-used Charm that makes it easier to kill Anathema, that's one of the key tenets their whole society is ordered around.<br /> <br /> But then you dig a little bit deeper, and it unfolds like a blossom. If you actually look at the Charm, it doesn't really specify that it be invoked with killing intent or only in combat <i>against</i> an Anathema, does it? Plenty of Charms can have explicit social cues, mental states, and situations which are required for them to &quot;fire;&quot; that's usually the purview of social charms, but hacky hacky slash-slash Charms can have those as well. This one doesn't. Once you cut away all the social baggage from it, you realize you can use it in situations that have nothing to do with its ostensible raison d'etre.<br /> <br /> And that's because it's an ancient First Age Charm and used to have entirely different social baggage! The Dragon-Blooded used to fight alongside the Anathema, slaying enemies of creation and serving in their retinues and acting as elite shock troops. One of the common images of a really serious First Age curbstomp has always, in my mind, involved a big ball of Dragon-Blooded with a delicious Celestial Exalt filling in the center. They fought alongside Anathema, and given the natural Dragon-Blooded tendencies towards synergy and teamwork, it makes total sense they'd develop a Charm that makes them more awesome and more likely to live when wading through a bunch of Fair Folk in the retinue of their crazy-ass Dawn Caste boss.<br /> <br /> And then you get into the way that Charm was turned against the Solars, and the connotations involved in that inversion, and its this whole weird and awesome social history of the Dragon-Blooded Host all encapsulated in a single Charm.<br /> <br /> I love that. I love that so much.<br /> <br /> (Also, now I want to read a supplement called &quot;A Social History of Charms.&quot; I'm sure someone in-setting wrote it.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T12:25:20-07:00","id":466361,"title":"","content":"Yesss Mercushio, very well said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T12:27:11-07:00","id":466364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=466355#post466355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, now I want to read a supplement called &quot;A Social History of Charms.&quot; I'm sure someone in-setting wrote it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm sure someone in the Realm burned it.<br /> <br /> But I'd love to read it too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T13:57:47-07:00","id":467848,"title":"","content":"I think Dragon Blooded would be better off by mostly dropping Charms that let you combine effects for attacks or buff other people and focus more on an idea of how diversity in what Dragon Blooded are capable of mean that when a lot of them are working together, they can utilise complementary effects or chain together actions to keep hammering away at the problem. I like that image John once used where, if you have an Exalt who can zoom around in the water, you can send your Water Aspect after them to hit them just hard enough to send them out to the waiting Brotherhood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T14:15:24-07:00","id":467863,"title":"","content":"I would like to say the alearens from jim butchers codex alera are more what I would like to see from dragon bloods","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T14:33:03-07:00","id":467875,"title":"","content":"I should also say that I feel &quot;teamwork&quot; as a specifically Terrestrial thing expressed through their Charms doesn't really have a result worth the hassle. I think the significance of their numbers is better expressed through characterisation and presentation of a culture, ideas of what they <i>do</i> with their powers rather than what the powers are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T15:06:30-07:00","id":467896,"title":"","content":"I've actually had huge issues with players not doing anything teamwork related, to the point where I gave out a bunch of teamwork charms for free and made any charm that helped out an ally cost half motes rounded down. Oddly even with that incentive none of them none of them ever used them. I'm not sure if it's just my group or not, but spending a bunch of motes to power up your whole group and lean on eachother doesn't seem to be a thing people want to do. <br /> <br /> I think it's just that people don't want to be part of the Power Rangers they want to be part of the Avengers, which is more a thing that celestial exalted do. <br /> <br /> On the other hand as NPCs it works really well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T15:15:27-07:00","id":467898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=467896#post467896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's just that people don't want to be part of the Power Rangers they want to be part of the Avengers, which is more a thing that celestial exalted do.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/195976-why-would-a-solar-ever-use-evocations?p=207913#post207913\">This reminds me of a thing I wrote.</a> I wonder how much more people would enjoy a particular splat, or even the game in general, if they had a solid idea of the themes and stories that certain splats are intended to play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T15:51:52-07:00","id":467923,"title":"","content":"I have this image now, drawn from an action scene I once mentally composed of a Terrestrial commando team fighting a Lunar (while surrounded by a ring of supporting heavy infantry providing a pike wall), where their major strategy consisted of alternations between the group of setting up significant tactical actions while everybody else would provide support with quick, hard-hitting attacks to keep the Lunar off-balance, lining her up as a target and keeping her from getting a hit in, because it would take a variety of distinct heavy attacks with long set up times to bring a Lunar down, and the relative strength of a Lunar to the fragility of a Terrestrial would mean that it doesn't take many hits to seriously mess one up. So you've got something like the Wood Aspect needing time to prepare her tangling poison arrow attack, while everybody else uses generic shock tactics to keep the monkey off her back because one major hit will severely diable her and then a massive chunk of their strategy is gone. It's a very unpolished concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T17:44:43-07:00","id":468028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=467923#post467923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have this image now, drawn from an action scene I once mentally composed of a Terrestrial commando team fighting a Lunar (while surrounded by a ring of supporting heavy infantry providing a pike wall), where their major strategy consisted of alternations between the group of setting up significant tactical actions while everybody else would provide support with quick, hard-hitting attacks to keep the Lunar off-balance, lining her up as a target and keeping her from getting a hit in, because it would take a variety of distinct heavy attacks with long set up times to bring a Lunar down, and the relative strength of a Lunar to the fragility of a Terrestrial would mean that it doesn't take many hits to seriously mess one up. So you've got something like the Wood Aspect needing time to prepare her tangling poison arrow attack, while everybody else uses generic shock tactics to keep the monkey off her back because one major hit will severely diable her and then a massive chunk of their strategy is gone. It's a very unpolished concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems...too easy.<br /> <br /> For context the only two times in game that I've ever seen a Wyld Hunt take down a Solar, the first time was a crazy setup. For context it was a dawn coming to kick their asses with his small army of beastmen. First they got a realm legion of deserters to setup in the town, and their earth aspect with a warstrider and power bow to setup in a valley nearby. The town itself was built partially on a spar of first age architecture overhanging a waterfall. So they took half their firedust charges and hid them in the structural weak points of the spar, and the other half on the ridge above the warstrider. So when the battle began the wood aspect lured the Solar to the spar, got a daiklave ran through his chest and with his dieing breath set off the explosives, which sent the Solar and the spar crashing down to the bottom of the watefall, followed by half the town.<br /> <br /> Then he returned, very angry, to the battle by leaping from the bottom of the waterfall to the warstrider position, where he fought the strider and a few of it's guards before they blew the ridge, and sent it toppling down on him as well. That one took him a little longer to dig his way out of, after which he leaped back into the battle, killing another one of the brotherhood with a huge strike from the clouds. Eventually he was slain by a massive coordinated attack, including essence weaponry and immaculate martial arts where the very last attack brought him down.<br /> <br /> Just kind of getting in a big circle and having a knockdown brawl feels like it would go very, very badly for the DB commando team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T18:14:54-07:00","id":468053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just kind of getting in a big circle and having a knockdown brawl</div> </div> </div> </div> I can accept this as a reading of my choice in simplification for the sake of clarity. I think what I actually had in mind was... functionally similar to what you're elaborating there, although I think there are playable game design conceits behind not making it so invested and convoluted. Like, as a way to achieve the objective, it all seems pretty cool, but this sort of thing does need to consider how the majority of people are going to opt to and be capable of running a group of Dragon Blooded. Even if one could have the books successfully convey the procedure as you've suggested it (which probably wouldn't be in the Charms), I feel that the majority of people would read it as extremely frustrating (although it depends on how abstract the combat system is). Although I suppose that's a tension that needs to be handled throughout the line as a whole; between what the books are selling not only as the condition in which Terrestrials destroy Anathema, but also the ones in which the Lunars are trying to undermine them, since it would kind of suck to play a sworn brotherhood that gets caught in a microcosm of the Lunar endgame and is faced with a Lunar and goes down with no chance. I suppose recognising mechanics as not simulating the setting is a start point for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T20:39:08-07:00","id":468104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=468053#post468053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what the books are selling not only as the condition in which Terrestrials destroy Anathema, but also the ones in which the Lunars are trying to undermine them, since it would kind of suck to play a sworn brotherhood that gets caught in a microcosm of the Lunar endgame and is faced with a Lunar and goes down with no chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm having difficulty parsing this statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T00:55:02-07:00","id":468186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=467848#post467848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Dragon Blooded would be better off by mostly dropping Charms that let you combine effects for attacks or buff other people and focus more on an idea of how diversity in what Dragon Blooded are capable of mean that when a lot of them are working together, they can utilise complementary effects or chain together actions to keep hammering away at the problem. I like that image John once used where, if you have an Exalt who can zoom around in the water, you can send your Water Aspect after them to hit them just hard enough to send them out to the waiting Brotherhood.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the kind of thing where a team of wood aspects can lay down suppressing fire, forcing an Anathema to expend tremendous effort to not get turned into a pin cushion while a team of melee combatants take advantage of the gaps. All the while an earth aspect can use a combination of awareness and war charms to coordinate the teams to achieve maximum efficiency and tell them when and where they need to move to both stay alive and not let their quarry escape. Or maybe a sorcerer uses a terrestrial circle spell which summons a sphere of water around a target and then a team of water aspect archers just unload with bows and arrows into the sphere and take advantage of the inherent difficulties of dodging in water.<br /> Honestly, in spite of what I suggested earlier, I think that this is a much more meaningful expression of &quot;superior teamwork&quot; than &quot;this charm gives me bigger numbers when my siblings are patting me on the back&quot; powers of 2e. The only potential pitfall I could see is just the problems that occur from &quot;sure you could get this Water Exalt out of the water for your brotherhood to murderize, but you are a Terrestrial which means you will always be outclassed by everyone. So have fun flailing impotently as this water dude swims circles around you.&quot; The other problem is that specificity and lateral tactics are of no use against somebody who can parry a mountain and can use one charm to remove all penalties regardless of source. But this is just my experience with 2e talking again. I trust the devs to deliver on Terrestrials which are actually as capable in mechanics as they are in fluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T01:14:05-07:00","id":468205,"title":"","content":"From what has been said about Gambits, I'm thinking they will help a LOT in making those kinds of tactics happen in game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T01:38:18-07:00","id":468238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=468205#post468205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what has been said about Gambits, I'm thinking they will help a LOT in making those kinds of tactics happen in game.</div> </div> </div> </div>*raises hand* What are Gambits? I've read the entire What We Know wiki and not seen anything about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T02:33:09-07:00","id":468257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having difficulty parsing this statement.</div> </div> </div> </div> The idea that Lunars are widely fighting against the Realm by trying to undermine its infrastructure so that they can't support things like armies and ancient weapons that Dragon Blooded have a certain dependence on is really cool, but it shouldn't come at the expense of scenarios where Outcastes with no army and no magic artillery get into a fight with a Lunar and win.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T05:21:05-07:00","id":468301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=465456#post465456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Terrestrial might can use a Charm to bolster one or more allies traits equal to his own. However, if it is used on another Dragon-Blooded, he may be able to reflexively activate the Charm as well (whether or not he has it) for a different trait. It gives a sense of...their powers don't just add together, they multiply!</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much exactly what I want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T05:30:00-07:00","id":468304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">First they got a realm legion of deserters to setup in the town,</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually interested in the context here. They got an entire realm legion to desert? Or they somehow found an entire legions worth of deserters and welded them back into a coherent realm-equivalent fighting force?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=468257#post468257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The idea that Lunars are widely fighting against the Realm by trying to undermine its infrastructure so that they can't support things like armies and ancient weapons that Dragon Blooded have a certain dependence on is really cool, but it shouldn't come at the expense of scenarios where Outcastes with no army and no magic artillery get into a fight with a Lunar and win.</div> </div> </div> </div>How many Outcastes, though?<br /> <br /> This is something that comes up a lot and there's no clear consensus. Most people seem to agree that all things being equal, a Lunar should eat a Dragon-Blood for breakfast, perhaps literally. But where's the breakpoint? You specify no armies and no magic artillery, which basically means &quot;guys in armor with daiklaves and/or powerbows.&quot; Should five Dragon-Blooded be able to take a Lunar? Ten? Twenty? How are we defining &quot;win&quot; here? If the Lunar constantly runs away but they'll get their clock cleaned in a straight fight, and the Dragon-Blooded can't do shit because someone who can turn into animals that use badass Strength/Athletics Charms is basically uncatchable, is the Lunar winning? Are the DBs? Is it fair or unfair if there are Lunars who can stealth in close enough to conduct a major alpha strike that completely murders the fuck out of a single DB, and then they fly away until they recover enough essence to do it again?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T05:55:41-07:00","id":468345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=468304#post468304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most people seem to agree that all things being equal, a Lunar should eat a Dragon-Blood for breakfast, perhaps literally. </div> </div> </div> </div>My problem with this notion is that it is absolute, lacking context. And the context makes all the difference. There are certainly situations where a lone DB completely owns a lone Lunar. There are certainly situations where a lone Lunar obliterates a larger-than-reasonable number of DBs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T06:23:11-07:00","id":468354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=468345#post468345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with this notion is that it is absolute, lacking context. And the context makes all the difference. There are certainly situations where a lone DB completely owns a lone Lunar. There are certainly situations where a lone Lunar obliterates a larger-than-reasonable number of DBs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence my qualifier, &quot;all things being equal.&quot; It's impossible to get there absent some kind of perfectly constructed arena, of course. Even a white room isn't &quot;equal&quot; because you're taking stunts out of the equation. But you can generally rough out an idea of it, can you not?<br /> <br /> It is true that something like &quot;an Elder DB stumbles across a Lunar who Exalted twenty seconds ago&quot; is going to result in that Lunar completely being obliterated, and &quot;Raksi somehow gets loose inside the Spiral Academy dormitories at three in the morning, filled with sleeping teenage untrained Dragon-Blooded&quot; is going to result in her having a colossal DB body count.<br /> <br /> But those are obviously edge cases, are they not?<br /> <br /> Also, I find it wearying to have to type out a long string of qualifiers and caveats every time I make a statement. &quot;A Lunar should generally eat a Dragon-Blood for breakfast&quot; seems like it ought to automatically carry with it the rhetorical weight of &quot;obviously, there are times when this will not be case&quot; unless clearly specified otherwise. That's what the &quot;generally&quot; is for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T12:34:20-07:00","id":468624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=468238#post468238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*raises hand* What are Gambits? I've read the entire What We Know wiki and not seen anything about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they were mostly talked about in the current RPGnet Ask the Devs thread. Anyway, the actual rules have not been talked about, but apparently it covers the whole &quot;combat maneuvers&quot; thing (that is, the part of it that is not just represented by the ebb and flow of &quot;momentum&quot;). First, this seems to cover basic things like disarming an opponent, but also more cinematic/videogame stuff like disabling colossal monsters bit by bit.<br /> <br /> And, perhaps more importantly, it seems it is pretty easy to come up with new ones on the spot. In one playtest report from Eric Minton (if certain redacted terms are indeed Gambits like I strongly suspect), a Gambit is invented to represent pinning someone with [arrows or daggers, or don't recall exactly].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T13:59:00-07:00","id":468737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=468304#post468304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm actually interested in the context here. They got an entire realm legion to desert? Or they somehow found an entire legions worth of deserters and welded them back into a coherent realm-equivalent fighting force?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was actually a &quot;legion&quot; composed of all the deserters from the Tepet massacre. They'd ran off and formed a kind of mercenary company, mostly trying to hide the fact that they were former realm soldiers as best as they could, just in case anyone back home decided to follow through and come kill them all for insubordination. Fortunately 3/5 of the party was from house Tepet and they managed to convince them to let them use their one remaining warstrider and pilot. They didn't want to commit their whole force because not fighting Solars is part of a healthy lifestyle. Luckily just before his army arrived the legion's Dragonlord basically said fuck it, this is the way to get back the honor they all lost when they ran away, and came to defend their village.<br /> <br /> They armed themselves with a poison that the party got from a local tribe, who in turn was wiped out for not joining the Dawn's warband, and landed a pyrrhic victory against the tiger warrior trained beastmen and their human allies. This was in addition to the dragon armor that they unlocked in the ruins beneath the town and the fortifications/traps they set up all over the place. I think they spent something like 7-8 sessions just preparing for this battle alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T15:55:48-07:00","id":468908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=468238#post468238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*raises hand* What are Gambits? I've read the entire What We Know wiki and not seen anything about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The cards <i>are</i> being played close to the chest. Not that much has been revealed because even the name has only recently been dropped.<br /> <br /> Apparently <i>Gambits</i> are something that emerged from the development of the new combat system that caused the promised martial art <i>Techniques</i> to be ditched; because Gambits did everything that Techniques were intended to do without requiring writing up highly-circumstantial &quot;moteless charm&quot; trees. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=468624#post468624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they were mostly talked about in the current RPGnet Ask the Devs thread. Anyway, the actual rules have not been talked about, but apparently it covers the whole &quot;combat maneuvers&quot; thing (that is, the part of it that is not just represented by the ebb and flow of &quot;momentum&quot;). First, this seems to cover basic things like disarming an opponent, but also more cinematic/videogame stuff like disabling colossal monsters bit by bit.<br /> <br /> And, perhaps more importantly, it seems it is pretty easy to come up with new ones on the spot. In one playtest report from Eric Minton (if certain redacted terms are indeed Gambits like I strongly suspect), a Gambit is invented to represent pinning someone with [arrows or daggers, or don't recall exactly].</div> </div> </div> </div>Greater flexibility; less bloating. <br /> <br /> Sounds good to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T18:46:23-07:00","id":469050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=468908#post468908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greater flexibility; less bloating.<br /> <br /> Sounds good to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds cool. So is there now no real reason to go MA over Brawl though if you are mortal? Will Martial Arts give mortals access to better Gambits within a particular theme? I really hope they don't get rid of, &quot;I may be mortal, but my Tiger Style is strong&quot; as a character concept. I mean, I guess that we could just go back to, &quot;my stunts are all about my mortal Crane Style usage.&quot; I'm reading deep into things without a lot of info, so I am probably wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T02:27:19-07:00","id":469263,"title":"","content":"I demand Charm that will allow a Dragon-Blooded brotherhood to do a five-tier handstand followed by an elaborately choreographed introductory dance number that takes twenty five minutes.<br /> <br /> With speed line backgrounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T02:44:09-07:00","id":469268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=469050#post469050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds cool. So is there now no real reason to go MA over Brawl though if you are mortal? Will Martial Arts give mortals access to better Gambits within a particular theme?</div> </div> </div> </div>This might not be quite what you are thinking of, but my impression would be that mortal brawlers aren't worse exactly, it's more that the setting just assumes that a high rating in brawl achieved through the school of hard knocks and experience is probably rarer than high ratings of MA, which can be systematically trained.<br /> <br /> So for individuals there's no real reason to pick playing a master of MA, other than it being easier to stunt various moves that the player wants, while for STs there's maybe a slight assumption that schools of really powerful martial artists are generally more common than gangs of really strong brawlers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T03:16:46-07:00","id":469271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=469263#post469263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I demand Charm that will allow a Dragon-Blooded brotherhood to do a five-tier handstand followed by an elaborately choreographed introductory dance number that takes twenty five minutes.<br /> <br /> With speed line backgrounds.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ezrbyf6t9mY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ezrbyf6t9mY\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ezrbyf6t9mY\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ezrbyf6t9mY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> totally legit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T06:56:32-07:00","id":469305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=469268#post469268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This might not be quite what you are thinking of, but my impression would be that mortal brawlers aren't worse exactly, it's more that the setting just assumes that a high rating in brawl achieved through the school of hard knocks and experience is probably rarer than high ratings of MA, which can be systematically trained.<br /> <br /> So for individuals there's no real reason to pick playing a master of MA, other than it being easier to stunt various moves that the player wants, while for STs there's maybe a slight assumption that schools of really powerful martial artists are generally more common than gangs of really strong brawlers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can get behind that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T17:29:52-07:00","id":469684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=468737#post468737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was actually a &quot;legion&quot; composed of all the deserters from the Tepet massacre. They'd ran off and formed a kind of mercenary company, mostly trying to hide the fact that they were former realm soldiers as best as they could, just in case anyone back home decided to follow through and come kill them all for insubordination.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am stealing this.<br /> <br /> I am stealing the hell out of this.<br /> <br /> You're a good man, Doc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T10:51:17-07:00","id":471372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=468354#post468354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence my qualifier, &quot;all things being equal.&quot; It's impossible to get there absent some kind of perfectly constructed arena, of course. Even a white room isn't &quot;equal&quot; because you're taking stunts out of the equation. But you can generally rough out an idea of it, can you not?<br /> <br /> It is true that something like &quot;an Elder DB stumbles across a Lunar who Exalted twenty seconds ago&quot; is going to result in that Lunar completely being obliterated, and &quot;Raksi somehow gets loose inside the Spiral Academy dormitories at three in the morning, filled with sleeping teenage untrained Dragon-Blooded&quot; is going to result in her having a colossal DB body count.<br /> <br /> But those are obviously edge cases, are they not?<br /> <br /> Also, I find it wearying to have to type out a long string of qualifiers and caveats every time I make a statement. &quot;A Lunar should generally eat a Dragon-Blood for breakfast&quot; seems like it ought to automatically carry with it the rhetorical weight of &quot;obviously, there are times when this will not be case&quot; unless clearly specified otherwise. That's what the &quot;generally&quot; is for.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;generally&quot;, unfortunately, makes the statement so vague as to be completely without rhetorical value. If you took any one of the 300 or so Lunars at random, and pitted them against any one of the what, 30,000 DBs at random, sure, it's probably better to bet on the Lunar. But some of those matchups are a <i>lot</i> more likely than others. So, if we account for which characters are actually likely to encounter each other I don't know that it's necessarily clear cut. Or rather, some of those fights will be absurdly one-sided (in either direction) and others will be close, and honestly in aggregate I'm not sure because the terms are pretty nebulous. But then Plot comes along and says that anyone can encounter anyone at any time, so EVERYTHING goes out the window. In the context of a story a young Lunar could run into Memnon, or a bunch of Dynast teenagers might run afoul of Leviathan. Which side the PCs happen to be on probably has more to say about default assumption than your splats do!<br /> <br /> In short, there are just too many things under the blanket of &quot;all things&quot;. I get the desire to not caveat every single sentence to death, but some minimal amount of context would go a long way to clarifying your thoughts.<br /> <br /> Maybe, just maybe, in an established edition like 2.X where the fundamentals of combat are basically a solved problem, it's worthwhile to talk in those sorts of sweeping statements, when &quot;generally&quot; could reasonably be taken to mean something like &quot;both characters are roughly equally invested into the default combat kit on which general consensus has settled for their splat.&quot; But I don't know that we have enough information about the way the new rules work to know if it's even strictly true in the broadest sense anymore. Who-would-win-in-a-fight may be an even firmer &quot;it depends&quot; than it used to be, for all we know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 04-07-2015, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T14:32:59-07:00","id":471693,"title":"","content":"My houserule, if I had ever ran a 2e game, would have been, &quot;If you're a DB cool enough to hang out with Celestials, then you're cool enough that other DBs wanna hang out with you.&quot; In fact, you being the leader of a posse of Terrestrials is what gets you noticed by a group of Celestials.<br /> <br /> Of course, I was gonna headcanon that DB's can do all sorts of crazy shit if you get five of them together, like five DB sorcerers casting Sapphire Circle spells if they all work together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T20:55:11-07:00","id":472063,"title":"","content":"While it's cool how Terrestrial magic enhances each other and other Exalted, I always loved how the Terrestrial Reinforcement Excellency allows them to do the same with their Mortal followers:<br /> <br /> *You got a bunch of fresh-faced recruits, barely able to swing a sword the right way? One use of Melee Reinforcement, and you've got an entire unit of Jubei Yagyus for a scene!<br /> <br /> *A pack of soldiers who only know the basics of first aid? Apply the Medicine Reinforcement, and instant triage team!<br /> <br /> *Need help solving a murder? Drop some motes on the Investigation Reinforcement, and your junior detectives can canvas the crime scene and grill witnesses like pros!<br /> <br /> *The Performance Reinforcement can turn even the worst community theater troupe into a spectacle worthy of the greatest of Shakespeare!<br /> <br /> And so, and so forth. Hell, if anything, the Realm isn't a fantastic *enough* representation of what humans can do with various types of Craft, Lore, Bureaucracy, etc, under the Dragon-Blooded!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T20:59:05-07:00","id":472066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=467848#post467848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Dragon Blooded would be better off by mostly dropping Charms that let you combine effects for attacks or buff other people and focus more on an idea of how diversity in what Dragon Blooded are capable of mean that when a lot of them are working together, they can utilise complementary effects or chain together actions to keep hammering away at the problem. I like that image John once used where, if you have an Exalt who can zoom around in the water, you can send your Water Aspect after them to hit them just hard enough to send them out to the waiting Brotherhood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't this pretty much exist, though? There's a charm in TCA that lets a combat group of Terrestrials focus their power on one champion among them, who gains all their charms for the scene, or something like that. <br /> <br /> There's also that Charm in Dreams that works over an extended unit of DBs on the battlefield, and gives each one the charms of every DB that falls in battle, or something to that effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T16:48:35-07:00","id":473513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded#post465109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Derpinblooded?</div> </div> </div> </div>There <i>is</i> an &quot;I&quot; in this, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T16:52:07-07:00","id":473514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=473513#post473513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There <i>is</i> an &quot;I&quot; in this, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a term of endearment!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T22:40:11-07:00","id":476693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/465109-there-s-no-i-in-dragonblooded?p=472063#post472063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's cool how Terrestrial magic enhances each other and other Exalted, I always loved how the Terrestrial Reinforcement Excellency allows them to do the same with their Mortal followers:<br /> <br /> *You got a bunch of fresh-faced recruits, barely able to swing a sword the right way? One use of Melee Reinforcement, and you've got an entire unit of Jubei Yagyus for a scene!<br /> <br /> *A pack of soldiers who only know the basics of first aid? Apply the Medicine Reinforcement, and instant triage team!<br /> <br /> *Need help solving a murder? Drop some motes on the Investigation Reinforcement, and your junior detectives can canvas the crime scene and grill witnesses like pros!<br /> <br /> *The Performance Reinforcement can turn even the worst community theater troupe into a spectacle worthy of the greatest of Shakespeare!<br /> <br /> And so, and so forth. Hell, if anything, the Realm isn't a fantastic *enough* representation of what humans can do with various types of Craft, Lore, Bureaucracy, etc, under the Dragon-Blooded!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that was sort of a misapplication of the Excellency concept.<br /> <br /> It's easy to handwave away how supercharging yourself with Essence allows you to perform better within your limits, but with Terrestrial Ability Reinforcement, you're just straight up adding dots to folks; giving them knowledge and skills and reflexes and habits unlike anything they've ever had before.<br /> <br /> That seems like it deserves more flavor text to justify, as well as a more clearly defined ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}